  "course_description": "Taught in English. An interdisciplinary course intended to provide in-depth study of formative elements, influences, and movements in German-speaking culture(s). May be repeated for credit when topic varies.",
  "course_notes": "This course is required for all students who will participate in the 2027 Summer Study Abroad Program in Vienna. This one-credit course is designed to prepare students for the 54th Summer Study Abroad Program in Vienna by focusing on three central themes: 1. Logistical and practical information about preparing to study, live, and travel overseas. 2. Historical and cultural background on Vienna and its surrounding regions. 3. Theoretical and practical information on language acquisition, intercultural communication, and sociolinguistic competence. In addition to covering these three themes, the course also allows program participants the opportunity to get to know each other before the program starts. There will also be opportunities to meet with past program participants to learn about their experiences in both cities.",
